I finally did it! After a year and a half of playing, I finally
ascended!

The first few levels were fairly average, no altar, a couple of shops
with not much in. Left my dog on level 1, he was still alive on the
way back up! Never tamed another monster, I really don't like pets,
and I was planning on getting Stormy anyway. Did the mines first, the
altar was lawful and there were no magic lamps in minetown. Carried on
down to the bottom, picked up the luckstone and came back up to
minetown. Once I got there, I brought a scroll of identify and read
it, it identified all my stuf for me, including a 0:2 wand of wishing
I must have picked up somewhere! This gave me +2 SDSM, +2 speed boots,
a +2 CoMR and +3 Stormbringer, the watch captain also gave me gloves
so I could weild a cockatrice corpse and a silver saber which I
enchanted and twoweaponed with Stormy.
Sokoban gave the bag of holding, which was very nice to have.

The first altar I found was on lvl 18, where I made holy water and
blessed my stuff. I started to sacrifice corpses hoping for another
weapon, but didn't realize it was a bad idea to offer dopplegangers
until Jubilex was standing next to me. Quickly unwielded Stormbringer
and took him up to lvl 17, where he stayed for the rest of the game.
Stopped sacrificing afer that, as I didn't really need another weapon.
A bones pile on lvl 25 gave me rings of slow digestion and conflict, a
magic marker and +2 Magicbane, which I never used. With the magic
marker I enchanted Stormy to +6 and my saber to +4, also some of my
armour.

The castle wand gave me a magic marker, +2 helm of telepathy, 2
scrolls of genocide, a ring of levitaiton, another +2 CoMR (my first
one got lost to a scroll of destroy armour), +3 Gauntlets of power and
a blessed spellbook of magic mapping for Gehenomm. The only spells I
cast were magic mapping and identify, as I had to take off my GoP and
CoMR and put on a robe. Genocided h's and L's.

I got through Gehennom fairly easily, whacking everything with my +6
Stormy and +4 silver saber, although I had to genocide disenchanters
as well after they kept taking my saber down to +1. The Wizard went
down to a wand of death, as did the priestess of moloch. Ditched the
Book of the Dead in the sanctum as it was making me burdened, and
started up again. Got delayed in Jubilex's swamp, thinking I'd lost
the stairs :-(. Met the Wizard several times on the way up, killed him
with my wand of death or a cockatrice corpse. Had a terrible urge to
take a statue of him with me, but couldn't manage it.

Of the planes, air was by far the hardest, with those elementals after
me. Got through earth with wands of digging, fire and air with my =oL.
Bit suprised when an Angel appeared next to me, but it stayed out of
my way. Killed Famine with a wand of death, never saw the other two.
Headed for the nearest door, it was an aligned altar and so I offered
up the amulet!



